WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:02.133
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.133 --> 00:00:03.200
Welcome, welcome, welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.300
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.467
Thank you for being here.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:07.567
Guys, I'm very excited
about this.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:09.968
James Corden
is my guest tonight.

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:11.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.467
♪♪

00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:15.734
He was supposed to be here
a few days ago,

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.367
but he took a carpool
all the way from L.A.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:21.100
Of course, since two
of the three late-night Jimmys

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.467
are in the same building,

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:24.834
Jimmy Kimmel is being locked
away in a secure location,

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.200
just so you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.300
I'm in a great mood
because we're right

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:28.734
in the middle
of the holiday season.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.501
Christmas is almost here.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:33.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.968 --> 00:00:36.501
And Hanukkah starts on Sunday.

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:39.467
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.534
Hanukkah is celebrated
for eight nights,

00:00:41.534 --> 00:00:43.267
so the next time you complain
about your relatives

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:45.033
at Christmas,
times that by eight.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.334
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.033
Of course, people are still
shopping for presents,

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:49.334
and I heard that, this year,

00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:52.601
one of the most unwanted gifts
is beauty products.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:53.901
That makes sense.
You can't hand someone

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:55.901
a bag of make-up like,
"I thought you needed this."

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:57.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.868 --> 00:00:59.968
Well, in a recent survey,
for the second year in a row,

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.601
New Hampshire ranked
as the state

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.834
with the most Christmas spirit.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.267
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.167
Vermont was like,
"Excuse me.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.667
We have the
Ghost of Christmas Past.

00:01:09.667 --> 00:01:10.968
Hello."

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:14.634
I mean, come on.

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:17.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.400
Let's get to some news.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.367
Last night, several
high-profile journalists

00:01:20.367 --> 00:01:21.901
who have been covering Elon Musk

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:24.367
had their
Twitter accounts suspended.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.801
Elon said the journalists
were using social media

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.300
to keep track
of what he's doing,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.767
or as that's also known,
social media.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:33.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.467
I have a feeling that,
right after Christmas,

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:37.234
we're gonna see Elon Musk in
line trying to return Twitter.

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:39.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:41.334
It's a big weekend for sports,
'cause this Sunday

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:46.467
is the World Cup final
between Argentina and France.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.067
Argentina and France.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.434
Of course,
my bracket's already busted.

00:01:49.434 --> 00:01:51.300
I had England and Gonzaga
in the final.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:54.234
Yep, Argentina versus France.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:55.567
At first, I wasn't sure
what was at stake,

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:56.634
but then someone told me

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.133
it's like "Evita"
versus "Les Mis."

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.501
And I was like, "Oh, I get it."

00:01:59.501 --> 00:02:00.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:03.267
The final will be played
on Sunday at 10:00 a.m.,

00:02:03.267 --> 00:02:05.234
so if you want to know
why soccer isn't more popular

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.801
in America, there's your answer.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:09.167
Well, everyone's
talking about this.

00:02:09.167 --> 00:02:11.968
13 years after the original,
"Avatar: The Way of Water"

00:02:11.968 --> 00:02:14.100
has finally hit theaters.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.834
Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.834 --> 00:02:18.133
This is wild.

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:20.901
The movie has a run time
of 3 hours and 12 minutes.

00:02:20.901 --> 00:02:22.067
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.701
That's not a movie,
that's a flight.

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.901
Even Hanukkah is like, "Whoa.
How long we doing this?"

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.300
If this was on Netflix,
the "Are you still watching?"

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:32.133
thing would pop up 48 times.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:34.601
"Yeah, I'm still watching."

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.067
I read that, this weekend,
screenings of

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:37.667
"Avatar: The Way of Water"
are selling out

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.267
all across the country,
especially at IMAX theaters.

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.901
And I think I know why.
Check out this ad I just saw.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:46.267
-You've never seen anything like
the underwater world of Pandora.

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.667
And in honor of
"Avatar: the Way of Water,"

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.133
IMAX has something else
you've never seen before.

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.033
Introducing FLYMAX,

00:02:53.033 --> 00:02:56.400
the first large-format urinal,
designed to handle your stream

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.400
after a 44-ounce Icee
and a 3-hour movie about water.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.567
Just zip and let 'er rip
as a cascade of blue liquid

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:06.267
take yours urine on
the adventure of a lifetime.

00:03:06.267 --> 00:03:07.434
-Whoo!

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.334
FLYMAX, by IMAX.

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:11.400
Putting the "Aaa" in "Avatar."

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:12.634 --> 00:03:13.834
-Yeah, that makes sense.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:16.767
[ Applause ]

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.200
Some business news --
for the next three days,

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:22.834
Starbucks union members
will strike at 100 locations.

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.434
Yep, on the other hand,
that means the other

00:03:24.434 --> 00:03:26.634
40,000 Starbucks will still
be open for business.

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:27.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.934 --> 00:03:29.934
Did you guys see this?
A Panera customer went viral

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:32.100
on TikTok after she discovered
that the chains

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:33.767
charged lemonade drink

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:36.167
contains more caffeine
than four espressos.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.334
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:38.601
Panera was like,
"Well, you're gonna to need it

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.167
after eating a mac-and-cheese
bread bowl."

00:03:40.167 --> 00:03:41.634
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.634 --> 00:03:44.601
After a few sips, she was like,
"Do you also hear EDM music?

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:45.968
Oh, never mind.
That's just my heart."

00:03:45.968 --> 00:03:47.767
♪ En, en, en, en, en,
en, en, en, en ♪

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.033
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:51.300
Guys, finally,
we have exactly one show left

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.334
before we go on Christmas break,
which means it's time for

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:54.968
that beloved
"Tonight Show" tradition.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.567
It's time for
"12 Days of Christmas Sweaters."

00:03:57.567 --> 00:03:59.200
Here we go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.601
-♪ 12 Days
of Christmas Sweaters ♪

00:04:01.601 --> 00:04:06.200
♪ One day left ♪

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:09.400
-That's right!
For each of the last 12 shows

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.133
before Christmas, we've been
giving one lucky audience member

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:13.834
a magnificent Christmas sweater

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.567
from the
Countdown to Christmas Cabinet.

00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:20.534
So since there is one show left,
let's open door number 1.

00:04:20.534 --> 00:04:22.234
Where are we?

00:04:22.234 --> 00:04:23.667
-It's right over there.
-Here?

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:24.667
-Right here.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:25.868
-Go for it, pal.
Ready?

00:04:25.868 --> 00:04:27.901
[ Drumroll ]

00:04:27.901 --> 00:04:29.033
Whoa!

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:31.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:34.634
♪♪

00:04:34.634 --> 00:04:35.834
[ Applause ]

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.567
It comes with a hat.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:40.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
Comes with a hat, too.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.367
Wow.
Okay.

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:45.133
Wow.

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:49.701
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:51.234
Now let's see --

00:04:51.234 --> 00:04:53.267
Now let's see who's going home
with tonight's sweater.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:54.767
Everyone look
at your seat number.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:57.801
If I call your number -- if I
call your number, come on down.

00:04:57.801 --> 00:04:59.767
Quest, could I get
a drumroll, please?

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:03.467
[ Drumroll ]

00:05:03.467 --> 00:05:05.567
238!

00:05:05.567 --> 00:05:06.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yes! Come here!

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.300
Come on down.

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:16.567
♪♪

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.200
Yes!

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:19.901
Hello!
How you doing?

00:05:19.901 --> 00:05:21.033
-Good. How are you?
-Nice to see you.

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.133
You can stand over there.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.200
Hi.
What is your name?

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.801
-Mikayla.
-Mikayla, where are you from?

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.200
-I'm from Nashville.
-Hey!

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.734
Nashville in the house!

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.968
It can get cool sometimes at
nighttime in Nashville, right?

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.067
-Yep.
-Do you have anything

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:35.968
like this at home?
-I don't think so.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.367
-How about the matching beanie?

00:05:37.367 --> 00:05:38.534
Do you have anything like that?
-Nope.

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:39.934
-Would you like to try it on
for our audience?

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.501
-Oh, of course.
[ Cheers ]

00:05:41.501 --> 00:05:43.901
-Do you want me to hold
your glasses or you got it?

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.968
You can han-- All right.
Mikayla, good job.

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.267
Be careful.

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:48.267
♪♪

00:05:48.267 --> 00:05:49.300
-Oh, perfect.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.133
[ Cheers ]

00:05:51.133 --> 00:05:56.100
♪♪

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:57.334
-There we go.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:06:00.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:01.234
-Thank you.

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:02.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.167
-Thank --
She wants to get out of it.

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:07.367
She's running away.
Bye, Mika--

00:06:07.367 --> 00:06:09.167
Wow, look at Mikayla
going up the stairs.

00:06:09.167 --> 00:06:12.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:16.267
[ Laughing ]

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.067
She was running away!

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:20.100
"Thank you very much!"

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.601
Running away from me.

00:06:21.601 --> 00:06:23.000
Yeah, it's like,
"Thank you, I'm so happy.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.834
Thanks for the sweater."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.234
You know what, though?
You know what, guys?

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:27.767
I'm in the giving spirit.

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:30.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:30.133 --> 00:06:31.968
Why --

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:33.868
Why does just one person
get a gift?

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:36.133
Why can't everyone
in the audience get a gift?

00:06:36.133 --> 00:06:37.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:38.601
That's right!

00:06:38.601 --> 00:06:40.868
It's time for "Tonight Show
Stocking Stuffers"!

00:06:40.868 --> 00:06:41.934
Here we go!

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:43.467
-♪ It's "The Tonight Show" ♪

00:06:43.467 --> 00:06:44.801
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:06:44.801 --> 00:06:46.467
-♪ It's "The Tonight Show" ♪

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:47.601
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:06:47.601 --> 00:06:50.367
-♪ Stocking Stuffers ♪

00:06:50.367 --> 00:06:52.601
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:52.601 --> 00:06:54.033
Every night
until Christmas break,

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:55.467
we're giving away
an awesome gift

00:06:55.467 --> 00:06:57.133
to every single person
in our studio audience.

00:06:57.133 --> 00:06:59.467
And we saved
the biggest gift for last.

00:06:59.467 --> 00:07:01.067
You guys ready for this?

00:07:01.067 --> 00:07:02.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:04.467
Questlove,
can I get a drumroll, please?

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:07.801
[ Drumroll ]

00:07:07.801 --> 00:07:11.767
Tonight's Stocking Stuffer is...

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:17.100
a SONDORS Smart Step
ReCycled e-bike!

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.667
Higgins.
-That's right, Jimmy.

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:22.567
SONDORS refurbished Smart Step
is an easygoing e-bike

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:25.234
delivering convenient design,
tech, and performance,

00:07:25.234 --> 00:07:27.133
while helping to maintain
a greener future

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:29.067
by keeping them out of
the landfills.

00:07:29.067 --> 00:07:30.434
With its
easy-step-through frame,

00:07:30.434 --> 00:07:31.934
the SONDORS
refurbished smart bike

00:07:31.934 --> 00:07:34.334
is as fun as
it is effortless to ride.

00:07:34.334 --> 00:07:36.801
Jimmy!

00:07:36.801 --> 00:07:39.100
-Everyone's getting an e-bike!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:42.567
Everyone's getting an e-bike!
Thank you, SONDORS!

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:44.200
Enjoy your gift, everybody!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:47.467
We'll be right back with more of
"The Tonight Show"!

